  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The function \(f\) is given by \(f(x)=10x+3\), and the function \(g\) is given by \(g(x)=2^x\). For each question, show your reasoning.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Which function reaches 50 first? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(f(5)=53\) and \(g(5)=32\), so \(f\) reaches 50 first. </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Which function reaches 100 first? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(f(7)=73\) and \(g(7)=128\), so \(g\) reaches 100 first. </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
